# Line endings — the installer runs on Linux.
#
# offline/install.sh is executed by an operator on an air-gapped host. A CRLF
# checked in from a Windows clone makes the shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`,
# and the only symptom is "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — a
# message that says nothing about line endings, on a machine with no internet
# to look it up from. Pin it rather than rely on everyone's core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Compose, edge config and workflows are read by Linux tooling too.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf

*.md text
*.env text
config.env.example text eol=lf
